<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nördlingen (1634)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1634</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Nördlingen, fought on 6 September 1634 in Swabia, was a crushing victory of the imperial and Spanish armies under the future Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand III</a> and the Cardinal-Infante Ferdinand over the Swedes and their German allies under Gustav Horn and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-of-saxe-weimar">Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</a>. It broke Swedish power in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-prague-1635">Peace of Prague</a> in 1635 and drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> openly into the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nordlingen-1634.jpg" alt="Battle of Nördlingen (1634)" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan van den Hoecke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_van_der_Hoecke_-_The_Battle_of_N%C3%B6rdlingen,_1634.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
